 ('Documentation baseline diff is a same-checkout comparison','audit_docs.py overlays changed prior content onto the current discovery set.',[P+'audit_docs.py'],'Existing discovered files are compared against prior text, not a complete historical tree. New/deleted docs can fail gitshow or change discovery, and prior.get evaluates read eagerly. Treat it as limited changed-document comparison, not full historical census.'),
 ('Frozen Instrument candidates preserve hashes without building','freeze.py explicitly freezes already-built WASM/native artifacts.',[P+'freeze.py'],'One commit and clean tracked runtime paths do not independently bind artifact compilation to source. Prior candidate source paths are unioned for browser input coverage; native list is separately reconstructed. Keep original build receipts beside frozen hashes; build/execution flags are explicitlyfalse.'),
 ('Instrument collector records several real invariants but trusts selected manifest facts','collect checks8browser runs, errors, adapter, native process/scenario frames, image variation and source stability.',[P+'collect.py'],'Color-count and two pixel checks are limited visual evidence; captured labels/source/binary facts are not rebuilt here. Collector copies all historical rounds and overwrites destination artifacts with dirs_exist_ok, so this audit did not rerun it. browser_closed depends on Q465 finalizer.'),
 ('Native Instrument runtime owns serial child processes and fresh libraries','run-native.py hashes candidate inputs, requires unlocked console and fresh per-case libraries.',[P+'run-native.py',P+'run-cpu.py'],'Structured commands, bounded child waits and inhibitor cleanup are real. Hardcodedcompiler/platform/target paths make these dated macOS runners, not portable current qualification. CPU gate script checks real command exits then metadata edges, not source-read coverage.'),
 ('Instrument browser checks scenarios but cleanup verdict drifts','verify-browser.cjs verifies scenario result, gate failures, page errors, visible document and stable session.',[P+'verify-browser.cjs'],'Real headed-driver checks are present. Cleanup catches errors yet claims closure, Q465. Probe records only that callback defect; historical acceptance not rerun. Browser source/package hash verification remains separate from native candidate provenance.'),
 ('Link history and opened-link fixtures preserve explicit owner selection','P2/P3 scenarios assert held/history scope, stable handles and unchanged selected detail/forme/accesses.',['support/receipts/link-model-knot-20261015/browser/p2_tree_link_history.scn','support/receipts/link-model-p3-20261016/browser/p3_tree_opened_link.scn'],'P3 repeats most P2 script assertions with additional timeline/list lanes. Copying preserves readable snapshots but invites fixture drift; same shape/count observations alone do not prove live lifecycle or source revision behavior. Source read, no scenario execution.'),
 ('Qualification server is a loopback collector, not an acceptance authority','Server packages static inputs, writes posted scenario progress/captures and invokes an explicit local resource fixture.',['support/receipts/link-model-p7-20261016/qualification_server.py'],'Receipts are client-supplied JSON, saved without adjudicating success. Package traversal is bounded; POST body64MiBcap and owner process timeout30s exist. Repeated labels/capture names overwrite files. Caller must provide fresh output and validate result/source. No server run.'),
 ('Typography verifier checks frozen evidence, not current rendering','verify.py hashes listed files/PNGdimensions and checks stored scenario/process/totals/durability statements.',['support/receipts/tabard_typography_20261012/verify.py'],'Its docstring correctly says no runtime launched. Several checks are recorded facts rather than independently recomputed durability/manual-review evidence; native process records compared to claimed binaryhash. Do not transfer this frozen proof to changed source.'),
 ('Resident wrappers copy process/profile logic and admission gaps','Three PowerShell scripts implement independent GPU sampling, timing and test launch.',[W+'inference_stages.ps1',W+'layer_streaming.ps1',W+'weight_formats.ps1'],'Whole-GPU scope disclaimers are honest; sampling misses some short peaks and stages can have zero GPU samples. Q422extends zero namedtest admission; Q463empty freshJSON success. Streaming/formats share almost identical Read-GpuMemory and supervision code rather than one verdict/measurement helper.'),
 ('Transport catalog separates proposed profiles from authority','71specs25profiles explicitly assert no conformance, incomplete closure/errata and separate application admission.',['support/standards/transport_catalog.toml','support/standards/prior_art.toml'],'Parsed counts, unique IDs and internal source/profile/spec links resolve. These dated source tables do not prove current external RFC/vendor/license facts or completed local campaigns. No external sources fetched in this source-review batch.'),
 ('Transport profiles preserve original object and policy ownership','Carrier, FEC, courier and hardware selection are separate slots; extra receipts never grant application author authority.',['support/standards/transport_catalog.toml'],'P2panda CBOR source versus Postcard release prose discrepancy is explicitly retained. Codec alternatives mutually exclude per transfer, rather than inventing one universal network runtime. Standards/profile repetition is declarative authored data; code consumers and compliance proof remain separate.'),
 ('Image comparator reports numeric verdicts without failing the process','compare.py computes full-frameRGBRMS,maxRGB,alpha deltas for3named captures.',[B+'integration-20261014/compare.py'],'It prints pass=false while naturally exiting0. This can be a diagnostic API if callers parse rows; not treated as a confirmed broken gate absent a caller contract. Size mismatch falls to failure defaults. No new image comparison ran.'),
 ('WASM size attribution is a partial parser and name heuristic','wasm_sizes.py parses import/code/name sections, demangles optionally and groups by leading crate/generic-free family.',[B+'limits-followup-20261014/wasm_sizes.py'],'Code bytes exclude section/length/import/other overhead; output is not total artifact bytes. Missing bounds/LEB/version validation and multi-memory/table type assumptions limit malformed/new module inputs. Demangler exit is not checked. Diagnostic tool, not a runtime compiler or full Wasm verifier.'),
 ('Browser negative fixtures drive concrete presentation failure seams','Fixtures inject createShader,texImage2D,gesture and delayed fallback failures and assert cleanup/retry observations.',[p for p in paths if p.startswith(B+'review/fixtures/')],'These are separately packaged controls against generated modules, with explicit result=fail reporting. Most only prove WebGL2 seams, some polling has no fixture-local deadline. Source reading does not renew actual browser receipts or infer device/backend parity.'),
 ('Cleromancy cold-owner sampler has a limited observational result','sample-owner.py starts a pinned executable and samples a child after a release marker.',['testing/receipts/cleromancy-c6-intake-20261016/sample-owner.py'],'Prints child exit and sampled flag without making them process failure; no command/source/binary fresh binding. It is a historical profiler, not a correctness gate. Poll loop unbounded, sample chooses lastchild rather than a typed owner identity.'),
 ('Negative-control recipe mutates source and restores a captured historical copy','Tucket recipe checks exact initial backuphash, plants forbidden fallback, rebuilds, runs control, restores and rebuilds.',['testing/receipts/tucket-custody/run-negative-control.ps1','testing/receipts/tucket-custody/tucket-authority-clean.rs'],'Restorationhash and mtime repair are explicit. This audit read it only; rerunning would edit product/source and overwrite old evidence. Shared concurrent mutation would still be clobbered in finally; no ownership lock. Stabletarget/homepaths are historical lane inputs, not newly created audit infrastructure.'),
